  "question": {
    "text": "An atomic nucleus having low $n / p$ ratio tries to find stability by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "the emission of an $\\alpha$ -particle",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "the emission of a positron",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "capturing an orbital electron (K-electron capture)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "emission of a $\\beta$ -particle",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Emission of a positron results in the conversion of a proton into neutron, along with the release of neutrino. Thus, the number of protons decreases and of neutron increases, i.e. $n / p$ ratio increases and the nuclei becomes stable.\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0025_899dbe464460.png\">"
  }
